{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And he has been warned by its owners.</b> It used a plural expression. It intends to say that if it had two owners — both are liable to death, and they are not like two people who killed a person at once, who are exempt according to the one who says so (Bava Kamma 26a), for there they are exempt from death at the hands of man but liable by the hand of Heaven, whereas here too they are exempt from death at the hands of man but liable by the hand of Heaven. And as for the ransom, since it is monetary, they are liable even at the hands of man."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:32:08.611424069Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}